<title>USA: Walt Disney Co Q4 pro forma shr rises.</title>
<headline>Walt Disney Co Q4 pro forma shr rises.</headline>
<text>
<p>CONSOLIDATED STATEMENT OF INCOME</p>
<p>			    For The Quarter Ended September 30</p>
<p>		   (Unaudited; in millions, except per share data)</p>
<p>				    (Pro Forma)	   (As Reported)</p>
<p>				  1996	 1995	1996	1995</p>
<p>REVENUES		    $5,272     $4,690    $5,272     $3,124</p>
<p>COSTS AND EXPENSES	(4,414)    (4,016)   (4,414)   (2,627)</p>
<p>OPERATING INCOME	     858	  674	 858	  497</p>
<p>CORPORATE ACTIVITIES</p>
<p> AND OTHER		     (61)	(102)	(61)	(82)</p>
<p>NET INTEREST EXPENSE	(171)	(173)     (171)	 (9)</p>
<p>NET INCOME		    $354	 $221	$336	 $265</p>
<p>EARNINGS PER SHARE	 $0.52	$0.32     $0.49	$0.50</p>
<p>Wtd Avg Shrs		   685	  687	 685	  533</p>
<p>			    For The Fiscal Year Ended September 30</p>
<p>				   (Pro Forma)	    (As Reported)</p>
<p>				  1996	1995	 1996	1995</p>
<p>REVENUES		 $21,238   $18,949     $18,739    $12,151</p>
<p>COSTS AND EXPENSES   (17,574)  (15,524)    (15,406)    (9,685)</p>
<p>ACCOUNTING CHANGE	 (300)	 ---	(300)	  ---</p>
<p>OPERATING INCOME	 3,364     3,425	 3,033	2,466</p>
<p>CORPORATE ACTIVITIES</p>
<p> AND OTHER		  (249)     (255)	 (309)	(239)</p>
<p>NET INTEREST EXPENSE    (698)     (775)	 (438)	(110)</p>
<p>ACQUISITION-RELATED</p>
<p> COSTS			  ---	 ---	 (225)	  ---</p>
<p>NET INCOME		$1,350    $1,326	$1,214     $1,380</p>
<p>EARNINGS PER SHARE     $1.96     $1.94	 $1.96	$2.60</p>
<p>NET INCOME EXCLUDING</p>
<p>NON-RECURRING</p>
<p>  ITEMS (1)	     $1,533    $1,326	$1,534     $1,380</p>
<p>EARNINGS PER SHARE</p>
<p>EXCLUDING NON-RECURRING</p>
<p>  ITEMS (1)		$2.23     $1.94	 $2.48	$2.60</p>
<p>Wtd Avg shrs		 689	 685	   619	  530</p>
<p>(1)  The 1996 amounts exclude the impact of the SFAS 121 accounting change ($300) and acquisition-related costs ($225).</p>
<p>Pro forma results assume acquisition of ABC unit occurred at the beginning of the respective periods for which above information is presented.</p>
<p>Q4 EPS decreased two percent to $0.49, reflecting ABC's results from Feb 9, effective date of acquisition.</p>
</text>
